{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"orchestral-curious-foxterrier","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Problem\nThe expected dedicated-mount set is hardcoded per volume in three places: infra/terraform/user_data.sh, infra/scripts/check-mounts.sh (hardcoded /var/gerrit /var/lib/rebar/gate-scratch), and infra/scripts/observability.sh (DATA_MOUNT, GATE_SCRATCH_MOUNT). A third volume added later gets no metric and no alarm until someone writes it into each place by hand.\n\nSplit from the closed bug 1064-8c4a-f399-41de (its residual AC4); the refusal-inert part of that bug was fixed by be40fd250fd.\n\n## Approach\nMake the mount set data (one list, single-sourced from terraform) and have the periodic probe iterate it, so present and future volumes share one alarm. tests/unit/test_gate_scratch_volume_aa40.py already pins agreement between consumers and is the place to extend.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The expected mount set is declared once; check-mounts.sh and observability.sh read it rather than hardcoding paths.\n- [ ] A test adds a hypothetical third mount and shows the probe covers it without editing the scripts.\n- [ ] make verify exits 0.","id":"c400-fec0-a7bf-4755","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Expected gate-scratch mount set is written by hand in three places, so a new volume gets no metric or alarm"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793146438994930691,"uuid":"8c6237e4-a87c-44cb-a112-d81291ed4884"}